{"seq":13,"slug":"type-systems","title":"类型系统","stage":"DONE","category":"languages","chapterCount":4,"docCount":14,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems","rating":{"composite":3.93,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":5,"strategic":3.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"类型系统-简介\">类型系统 简介</h1><p>在每一门编程语言的背后，都默默运转着一套规则：它规定数据有哪些&quot;种类&quot;、哪些操作对哪些种类合法——这就是&quot;类型系统&quot;。一个整数能否与一段文本相加？一个对象上能否调用某个方法？答案都由类型系统裁定。它看似是语言的技术细节，实则深刻影响着程序的安全、表达力，乃至我们思考代码的方式。</p>\n<p>本知识库讲的是<strong>跨语言、语言无关的类型系统通论</strong>——那些在 TypeScript、Rust、Haskell、Go 里反复出现的同一批概念（静态/动态、强/弱、推断、多态、泛型、代数数据类型……），抽离出具体语法，讲清它们的本质、彼此的关系、以及背后的设计张力。读完它，你再去学任何一门语言的类型系统，都能一眼认出&quot;这是哪个概念的哪种取舍&quot;。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</h2><p>本库刻意<strong>不绑定任何一门语言</strong>。如果你想看某个概念在具体语言里怎么写、怎么用，请移步对应的语言 hub——本库负责&quot;是什么、为什么&quot;，语言 hub 负责&quot;怎么做&quot;。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>你的问题</th>\n<th>去哪个 hub</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>类型系统的通用原理、概念之间的关系、设计取舍</td>\n<td><strong>本 hub（类型系统）</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>这些概念在某门语言里的具体语法与工程实践</td>\n<td>该语言的 hub（见下表）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>类型系统作为&quot;语言特性&quot;该如何设计、取舍</td>\n<td><a href=\"../programming-language-design/semantics/type-system-design\">编程语言设计 · 类型系统设计</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>和类型/积类型、Option/Result、模式匹配的范式用法</td>\n<td><a href=\"../functional-programming/algebraic-types/sum-and-product-types\">函数式编程 · 代数类型</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>各语言 hub 与本库概念的对应关系：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>本库概念</th>\n<th>看它的具体落地</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>类型推断、渐进类型</td>\n<td><a href=\"../typescript/basic-types/type-annotations-and-inference\">TypeScript</a>、<a href=\"../ocaml-functional-systems/foundations/type-inference\">OCaml</a>、<a href=\"../python-advanced/type-system/type-annotations\">Python 注解</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>多态、泛型、类型约束</td>\n<td><a href=\"../rust-language/type-system/traits-and-generics\">Rust 特征与泛型</a>、<a href=\"../go-language/interfaces-and-generics/generics-in-go\">Go 泛型与接口</a>、<a href=\"../java-language/java-core-fundamentals/type-system-and-generics\">Java 泛型</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>代数数据类型、让非法状态无法表示</td>\n<td><a href=\"../rust-language/type-system/enums-and-pattern-matching\">Rust 枚举</a>、<a href=\"../haskell-pure-functional/type-system/algebraic-types\">Haskell 代数类型</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>类型安全、把资源纳入类型（前沿）</td>\n<td><a href=\"../rust-language/ownership-and-borrowing/ownership-rules\">Rust 所有权</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><ul>\n<li>会用至少一门编程语言写过非平凡的程序（有变量、函数、对象/结构的概念）。</li>\n<li>隐约体验过&quot;类型错误&quot;——比如把字符串当数字运算、调用了不存在的方法。</li>\n<li><strong>不需要</strong>任何特定语言或数学/类型论背景。本库全部用直观的语言和比喻讲解，不依赖任何一门语言的语法。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径\">推荐学习路径</h2><p>全库共四章，建议<strong>按章节顺序通读</strong>——后一章反复用到前一章的概念。</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>第一章 · 类型系统基础</strong>：什么是&quot;类型&quot;、类型系统起什么作用、以及&quot;静态 vs 动态&quot;这一贯穿全局的根本分野。</li>\n<li><strong>第二章 · 类型检查与安全</strong>：类型系统如何&quot;把关&quot;——类型检查如何运作、&quot;类型安全&quot;的真义、&quot;强 vs 弱&quot;。注意区分三组易混维度：何时检查（静态/动态）、是否捕获误用（安全/不安全）、多严格（强/弱）。</li>\n<li><strong>第三章 · 类型推断与多态</strong>：化解静态类型&quot;啰嗦&quot;的推断，与化解&quot;重复&quot;的多态/泛型/约束——现代静态类型既安全又好用的两大利器。</li>\n<li><strong>第四章 · 高级类型与意义</strong>：代数数据类型、&quot;让非法状态无法表示&quot;、类型系统的前沿，最终上升到类型作为设计与思维工具的深层意义。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>针对不同人群：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>只想快速建立全局观</strong>：读第一章三节 + 第四章末节《整体意义》，即可把握主线与三重身份。</li>\n<li><strong>写动态语言、想理解静态类型的好处</strong>：重点读第一章《静态 vs 动态》、第二章《类型安全》、第三章《类型推断》。</li>\n<li><strong>已用静态语言、想进阶</strong>：直接从第三章泛型/约束读起，再深入第四章代数数据类型与前沿。</li>\n<li><strong>学完概念想看落地</strong>：每篇末尾的&quot;延伸阅读与跨学科链接&quot;已为你指向各语言 hub 的对应实现。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>阅读时不妨把握一条主线：类型系统通过给数据划分&quot;种类&quot;、规定其上的合法操作，在编译期就拦截大量错误、并表达设计意图——它始终在&quot;安全与约束&quot;和&quot;灵活与简洁&quot;之间寻求平衡，既是防错的卫士，更是帮助我们精确建模、清晰思考的强大工具。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"type-system-foundations","title":"第一章 类型系统基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-system-foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"what-is-a-type","title":"什么是类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-system-foundations/what-is-a-type"},{"seq":2,"slug":"role-of-type-systems","title":"类型系统及其作用","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-system-foundations/role-of-type-systems"},{"seq":3,"slug":"static-vs-dynamic","title":"静态类型与动态类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-system-foundations/static-vs-dynamic"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-checking-and-safety","title":"第二章 类型检查与安全","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-checking-and-safety","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"how-type-checking-works","title":"类型检查的运作","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-checking-and-safety/how-type-checking-works"},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-safety","title":"类型安全","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-checking-and-safety/type-safety"},{"seq":3,"slug":"strong-vs-weak","title":"强类型与弱类型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/type-checking-and-safety/strong-vs-weak"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"inference-and-polymorphism","title":"第三章 类型推断与多态","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/inference-and-polymorphism","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"type-inference","title":"类型推断","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/inference-and-polymorphism/type-inference"},{"seq":2,"slug":"polymorphism","title":"多态","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/inference-and-polymorphism/polymorphism"},{"seq":3,"slug":"generics","title":"泛型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/inference-and-polymorphism/generics"},{"seq":4,"slug":"type-constraints","title":"类型约束与抽象","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/inference-and-polymorphism/type-constraints"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"advanced-types-and-significance","title":"第四章 高级类型与类型系统的意义","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/advanced-types-and-significance","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"algebraic-data-types","title":"代数数据类型与精确建模","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/advanced-types-and-significance/algebraic-data-types"},{"seq":2,"slug":"type-system-frontier","title":"类型系统的强大前沿","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/advanced-types-and-significance/type-system-frontier"},{"seq":3,"slug":"types-as-design-tool","title":"类型作为设计与思维工具","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/advanced-types-and-significance/types-as-design-tool"},{"seq":4,"slug":"significance","title":"整体意义","url":"/l-doc-books/h/languages/type-systems/advanced-types-and-significance/significance"}]}]}